# A Kafka broker on this machine. The quickest way to have one:
#
#   docker run -d --name kafka -p 9092:9092 apache/kafka:4.2.2
#
# The flow that uses this application listens with these same settings
# (`connection: orders` in its frontmatter), so this file is the only place the
# cluster is written. Add a staging.env -- with KAFKA_SASL_MECHANISM,
# KAFKA_USERNAME and KAFKA_PASSWORD if the cluster asks -- to run the same flow
# against staging.
KAFKA_BROKERS=localhost:9092

# Where the Avro schemas live, for the listener to decode Avro messages. JSON
# and text messages need nothing.
# KAFKA_SCHEMA_REGISTRY_URL=http://localhost:8081
# KAFKA_SCHEMA_REGISTRY_USERNAME=
# KAFKA_SCHEMA_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=
